# ---------------------------------------------------------------- people new in era 5
@char e5.tom_c
name: Tom Furrowe, housing inspector
speaker: TOM
faction: district
about: Thirty-three. Divorced, back at his mother's. A lanyard, a clipboard and a damp meter that beeps. Says well when he wants time.

@char e5.kit
name: Kit Furrowe
speaker: KIT
faction: district
about: Fifteen. Tom's daughter. Was in Ryan Haldane's form. Ines Saro sits behind her in Geography.

@char e5.jo
name: Jo Furrowe
speaker: JO
faction: district
about: Thirty-six. Tom's sister. A nurse on nights at the General. Was on the ward when they brought Danil up.

@char e5.leon_c
name: Sergeant Leon Brack
speaker: LEON
faction: district
about: Forty. Big, a knee that clicks, a wedding photograph with a crack in the glass. Says right before he does a thing.

@char e5.shaw
name: PC Shaw
speaker: SHAW
faction: district
about: Twenty-six. Leon's constable on the van. Says Sarge as a question.

@char e5.hale
name: Chief Inspector Hale
speaker: HALE
faction: district
about: Fifty-two. A runner. A plant on his windowsill somebody else waters. Thinks in how things read.

@char e5.mara
name: Mara Haldane
speaker: MARA
faction: hesh
about: Twenty-seven. Joss's granddaughter. The tenants' committee, a laminated lanyard, a spreadsheet of every call about the gutter.

@char e5.kev
name: Kev Haldane
speaker: KEV
faction: district
about: Forty-six. Lew's son, raised Tarn on the estate. Mara calls him cousin. Tarn United shirt. Two sausage rolls at a time.

@char e5.ryan
name: Ryan Haldane
speaker: RYAN
faction: district
about: Fifteen. Kev's lad. Thinks he's Tarn; has the black sheaf on his phone case. Delivered the committee's leaflets on his bike.

@char e5.ines
name: Ines Saro
speaker: INES
faction: vell
about: Fourteen. Danil's sister. Reads the comments aloud to her grandmother because her grandmother asked.

@char e5.frank
name: Frank Mott
speaker: FRANK
faction: district
about: Eighty. Walter Mott's grandson. Forty years a records clerk. His hands shake and he says it's not this.

@char e5.ellie
name: Ellie Ashby, the real Edrin
speaker: ELLIE
faction: district
about: Thirty-one. Paul Ashby's granddaughter. A channel, a ring light, a sponsor. Believes every word she says.

@char e5.sam
name: Dr Sam Lind
speaker: SAM
faction: district
about: Forty-six. GP, the vaccine centre on Tuesdays, the coroner's duty rota. Clara Lind's great-grandson.

@char e5.pryor
name: Dr Pryor, police surgeon
speaker: PRYOR
faction: district
about: Sixty-three. A voice for juries. Good at waiting.

@char e5.charlotte
name: Charlotte Orme
speaker: CHARLOTTE
faction: district
about: Forty-five. Victor's granddaughter. The ring-road syndicate and its model under perspex.

@char e5.dennis
name: Dennis Krall, chair of regeneration
speaker: DENNIS
faction: district
about: Fifty-five. Furrow League. Carpets. As a boy of ten he screamed on a chair at the mill fight.

@char e5.bev
name: Bev, family liaison officer
speaker: BEV
faction: district
about: Twenty-nine. A lanyard and a folder. Says I'm so sorry and means it every time.

@char e5.baker
name: Mr Lowe, the baker on Mill Street
speaker: BAKER
faction: district
about: Sixty-one. The bakery was his father's and his father's father's, when the Lowes were the Lowys. Talks about bread.

@char e5.dealer
name: Mr Hartley, the dealer
speaker: DEALER
faction: district
about: Sixty. Antiques and Clearances, on the hill. Dresses his window for every week the town has a name for.

@char e5.customer
name: A woman from the nail bar
speaker: CUSTOMER
faction: district
about: Drying her nails. Likes the table.

# the voices that carry the posts and the clip to the player, heard and never shown as text (weighted-devices pass,
# 2026-10-23: a post is a phone held out and read aloud, a voice message, a chant; design/device-audit/era5.md)
@char e5.fed
name: The Federation rep
speaker: FED
faction: district
about: Fifties, a fleece, a coffee. Has sat at a lot of kitchen tables. Knows the words that keep a man in a job.

@char e5.lad
name: A lad on a bike
speaker: LAD
faction: district
about: On his way to school down Mill Street. Reads out anything sprayed on a wall, the way kids do.

@char e5.league_man
name: A man's voice on the League's video
speaker: LEAGUE
faction: district
about: Slow and warm, like a man reading in church. Nobody has seen his face.

@char e5.phone_voice
name: The phone's reading voice
speaker: PHONE
faction: district
about: The voice for people who can't see the screen. Flat, polite, says the names wrong.

@char e5.eadie
name: Mrs Eadie, the coroner's officer
speaker: EADIE
faction: district
about: Fifty-eight. Takes the cause of death from the doctor's mouth to the family's door. Keeps her coat on.

@char e5.neighbour
name: The woman behind the net curtain
speaker: NEIGHBOUR
faction: district
about: Lives across Mill Street from the Saros' shop. Filmed it. Has not slept in her front room since.

