# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the clearance fight
# Story fight 2 (era5.md e5.s12). Placeholder ground and pattern until the combat lead builds q5_haldane_yard's arena
# and a bailiff pattern; every outcome goes to the same yard after, because the fate was decided at the door.
@encounter e.e5_door
name: The Haldane door
area: granary
boss: captain
win: e5.door.carried
yield: e5.door.carried
fled: e5.door.carried
down: e5.door.carried

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the fates, each with its decider
# f.e5_danil is the one canon fate: one way only, exempt from the two-outcome rule in tools/fatecheck.mjs (EXEMPT),
# with this reason: the canon hinge of era 5; the player's agency is in what follows (the certificate, the pages,
# the door), not in the death (DECISIONS-2026-10-22.md, era questions, item 4; commit e519930).
@fate f.e5_danil
pressure: has(e5.clip_open)
subject: household e5_saro
decider: LEON
scene: e5.clip.stop
window: 7
taken: yes
who: Danil
because: Tuesday's stabbing on Bridge Street and a description that said possibly Vell; Sergeant Leon Brack stops Danil Saro on Mill Street and kneels on him until he stops

@fate f.e5_cert
pressure: has(e5.cert_open)
subject: household e5_record
decider: SAM
scene: e5.cert.decide, e5.cert.true, e5.cert.false
window: 7
who: Danil
because: the police surgeon's words and a riot feared by Saturday; Dr Sam Lind looks at the flour in the boy's nails and says to the coroner's officer at the door compression of the chest and neck while restrained, or the surgeon's sudden death after exertion, cause unascertained, which is what she takes to the father

@fate f.e5_house
pressure: has(e5.vote_carried)
subject: household e5_haldane
decider: LEON
scene: e5.door.decide, e5.door.down, e5.door.cleared
window: 7
taken: yes
who: Mara
because: the vote, and the bailiffs' orange cross sprayed over the inspector's pink dot on the door; Leon Brack stands the van down till Monday when his mother puts Tomas's cap in his hands and says Will's words to him, or tells the bailiffs to go on

@fate f.e5_frank
pressure: has(e5.ledger_open)
subject: household e5_record
decider: FRANK
scene: e5.ledger.decide, e5.ledger.torn, e5.ledger.left
window: 7
who: Walter
because: the archive opening with his name on the door and the old exchange scale in its front room; Frank Mott brings Walter's iron wedge to Mara's table in his tobacco tin and says what it did under the barns' pan, then drops it off the bridge into the Edd (falls), or carries it up to the archive to go under the pan where it went

@fate f.e5_page_tom
pressure: has(e5.archive_open) & q_class == inspector
subject: household e5_record
decider: TOM
scene: e5.page.tom, e5.page.tom.lost, e5.page.tom.kept, e5.page.tom.given
window: 7
who: Tomas
because: the ring road's digger opens the wall of Tesk's old fold and Krall's office wants anything Hesh for its heritage panel; Tom Furrowe lets the child's oat sack with the blue goat go back into the spoil, bags it for the panel, or carries it to Sefa Tesk

@fate f.e5_page_leon
pressure: has(e5.archive_open) & q_class == militia
subject: household e5_record
decider: LEON
scene: e5.page.leon, e5.page.leon.lost, e5.page.leon.kept, e5.page.leon.given
window: 7
who: Tomas
because: the ring road's digger opens the wall of Tesk's old fold and Krall's office wants anything Hesh for its heritage panel; Leon Brack drops the child's oat sack with the blue goat into the bucket, gives it to the contractor's man for the panel, or carries it to Sefa Tesk

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the self-lies (each echoed word for word at the table)
@selflie e5.sl.says
about: SPITE, Everybody Says, armed for both lines by the share already on the player's phone (e5_town.lwd, e5.share); endured at the stone on the verge
happened: Danil Saro was walking home with a key on a shoelace and a bag of rolls. The story you sent on had a knife in it, or a heart. ? has(e5.danil_dead)
happened: The story was out before you woke. You were the one who sent it on to the people who trusted you.

@selflie e5.sl.order
about: LOYALTY, Order for Leon, three generations in the wall, at the account he gives the camera in his kitchen (e5_town.lwd, e5.trade.leon)
happened: Mill Street was quiet that night until the van stopped. The lad had his hands up before anybody touched him. ? has(e5.danil_dead)
happened: Nobody on Mill Street had a bat that night. There was a lad with bread, and a sergeant who stayed on.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- lore
@chain e5.street
name: The window across Mill Street
# the net curtain the clip was shot through, and the wall's answer, read out by a lad on his way to school
route: one-run | e5.lore.curtain, e5.lore.wall

@lore e5.lore.curtain
chain: e5.street
layer: surface
where: node e5.clip.stop
about: The first-floor window across Mill Street from the Saros' shop, with a net curtain. In the corner of the clip's first second, a woman's fingers holding the curtain back. Her name was never given to anybody.

@lore e5.lore.wall
chain: e5.street
layer: surface
where: node e5.stories
about: The ply over the Saros' boarded window, sprayed in the night in letters the height of a man, and read out loud by every kid going past to school: they killed him for walking home. By noon somebody had sprayed a line through killed.

@chain e5.clip
name: The whole four minutes
# the first seconds of the video, before the knee; and what the sergeant's knee felt. Each class can hold it in one
# run: the Inspector by the start and his sister on the ward, the Sergeant by his knee and the start played to him
route: two-classes | e5.lore.hands, e5.lore.knee
route: one-run | e5.lore.hands, e5.lore.ward
route: one-run | e5.lore.knee, e5.lore.start

@lore e5.lore.hands
chain: e5.clip
layer: hidden
where: node e5.cert.tom
requires: class inspector
about: The first seconds of the whole video, which the news never showed: a lad eating a roll on Mill Street, the van pulling across him, and both his hands going up, the paper bag in one, before anybody touched him.

@lore e5.lore.knee
chain: e5.clip
layer: hidden
where: node e5.trade.leon
requires: class militia
about: What the Federation's words leave out and Sergeant Brack's knee kept: the give under it when the lad stopped, and staying on after, and not getting up.

@lore e5.lore.ward
chain: e5.clip
layer: deep
where: node e5.dinner.furrowe
requires: class inspector
about: Jo on the ward when they brought him up, saying it at her mother's table: they knelt on him till he died for walking home.

@lore e5.lore.start
chain: e5.clip
layer: deep
where: node e5.office.leon
requires: class militia
about: The start of the window's video, played to the sergeant in an interview room, the first time he has seen it: the lad's hands going up, both of them, the paper bag in one, before anybody touched him.

@chain e5.books
name: The wedge and the sack
# Walter Mott's iron wedge in Frank's tobacco tin, and Dorrah Tesk's oat sack in the wall of the fold
route: one-run | e5.lore.margin, e5.lore.oats

@lore e5.lore.margin
chain: e5.books
layer: surface
where: node e5.ledger
about: Walter Mott's iron wedge, kept a hundred years in a tobacco tin: it went under the exchange scale's pan the famine winter so the barns' carts weighed heavy, and when a Haldane boy came to the scale about his father's carts, Walter sent him home.

@lore e5.lore.oats
chain: e5.books
layer: surface
where: node e5.fold
about: A child's oat sack with a goat stitched on it in blue thread, its head turned back, a few oats still in the seam, pushed into the wall of Tesk's fold a hundred years ago and opened by the ring road's digger.

@chain e5.carried
name: What was said at the kitchen table and at the door
# the carried words reach era 5: Nan to Tom over the clip, Ann to Leon at the Haldane door with the cap in his hands.
# Each class can hold it in one run: Tom carries the words to Ann's door; Leon has the cap off the nail and the words
route: two-classes | e5.lore.carry_f3, e5.lore.carry_b3
route: one-run | e5.lore.carry_f3, e5.lore.carry_fb
route: one-run | e5.lore.carry_b3, e5.lore.cap

@lore e5.lore.carry_f3
chain: e5.carried
layer: deep
where: node e5.dinner.f3
requires: class inspector
about: What Nan had from her mother in the hospice, and Ruth from Pell, and Pell from Ned on the step: I carried him. You don't need two for that. Will Brack's words, on the Crown's steps.

@lore e5.lore.carry_b3
chain: e5.carried
layer: deep
where: node e5.door.ann.words
requires: class militia
about: What Ann had from Davey in the kitchen over the Crown, and Davey from Will with his feet in a bowl: I carried him. You don't need two for that. Said by Ann to her son at the Haldane door, with the boy's brown cap off the Brack kitchen's nail in his hands.

@lore e5.lore.carry_fb
chain: e5.carried
layer: deep
where: node e5.fb.ann
requires: class inspector
about: Nan's words said on Ann Brack's step at night, by a Furrowe to a Brack, the way they came: and down the hall behind her, on a nail by the back door, a boy's brown cap.

@lore e5.lore.cap
chain: e5.carried
layer: hidden
where: touch q.brack_cap hold
requires: class militia
about: The boy's brown cap on the nail by the Brack kitchen's back door, small enough for a boy of eleven, that Will Brack took off the bench in the end cell and hung there, and that has never come down.

