# ---------------------------------------------------------------- props (era5.md section 7), new in era 5
# The five that persist from era 1 (the table, the bowls, the sign, the scale, the fence) are in q_props.lwd, standing
# where era 5's scenes are set (in:). These exist from era 5 only (from: 5). Each stands at a mark on its place's
# plate (render/props/e5_*.mjs, marks.spots). Weighted-devices pass, 2026-10-23: every prop is a thing the hands and the
# senses meet; three keep their ids with new things in them (q.mott_ledger is Frank's tobacco tin with Walter's wedge,
# q.tesk_book the archive's heritage case, q.clearance_order the Haldane door with its paint). DRAFT text (S14).
@prop q.clip
from: 5
name: The clip on a phone
place: q5_mill_street
mark: clip
tells: household e5_saro
verb: Look at the phone
carries: sound
state: 5 paused | The clip on a cracked phone screen, paused where everybody pauses it, at the knee. The phone keeps chiming in your hand, and chiming, as people send it on.
touch: listen "Hold the phone to your ear" | Under the chiming, very small, through the speaker, a lad saying he lives there. He says it again. {sense: e5.clip.sound}

@prop q.memorial
from: 5
name: The memorial
place: q5_square
mark: memorial
tells: era
carries: touch
state: 5 washed ? has(e5.commemoration) | The bronze sheaf, unveiled now, the villages in raised letters round the plinth, and no person's name anywhere on it. The step at its foot is wet and clean. Somebody chalked a word there last night and the council's jet wash had it off by eight.
state: 5 sheeted | The bronze sheaf under a tarpaulin, roped, waiting for the commemoration. Where the rope has slipped you can see raised letters along the bottom of the plinth, villages, and no person.
touch: wipe "Put your hand on the step" | Cold and wet from the jet wash, and gritty where the chalk was. Your palm comes up clean. {sense: room.cold}

@prop q.mott_ledger
from: 5
name: Frank Mott's tobacco tin
place: q5_mara_flat
mark: ledger
tells: household e5_record
verb: Look at the tin
carries: weight
state: 5 drowned ? has(e5.page_torn) | Frank's tobacco tin on Mara's windowsill, empty, the lid not quite shut. It still smells of his pipe, and under the pipe, of rust.
state: 5 tin ? has(e5.ledger_open) | A tobacco tin on Mara's table, older than anybody in the room, the paint worn through to the metal where a thumb opens it. It sits on the oilcloth heavier than a tin should.
state: 5 table | Mara's kitchen table under its oilcloth, wiped, the sugar in the middle, a burn mark by the edge from a pan.
touch: lift "Lift the tin" ? has(e5.ledger_open) & !has(e5.page_torn) | Heavier than a tin should be. Something inside shifts as you tip it and knocks against the side, once, iron on tin. {sense: e5.tin.set}

@prop q.tesk_book
from: 5
name: The heritage case
place: q5_archive
mark: tesk_book
tells: household e5_record
verb: Look at the case
carries: sight
state: 5 given ? has(e5.page_given) | The glass case for Krall's heritage panel, by the old scale in the front room, with a space on the green felt at the front that nothing has been put in. The spotlight in the lid shines on the felt.
state: 5 kept ? has(e5.page_kept) | The glass case by the old scale. On the green felt, a child's oat sack, coarse, mended at one corner, with a goat stitched on it in blue thread, its head turned back. Clay still in the weave. A spotlight on it.
state: 5 lost ? has(e5.page_lost) | The glass case by the old scale, empty, a square of green felt and a spotlight on nothing.
state: 5 waiting | The glass case by the old scale, new, empty, with a spotlight in its lid, waiting for whatever Krall's office wants put in it.
touch: press "Put your hand on the glass" | Cold. Your hand leaves a mark on it that fades in from the edges.

@prop q.haldane_five
from: 5
name: The envelope in the drawer
place: q5_mara_flat
mark: drawer
tells: household e5_haldane
carries: touch
state: 5 envelope | An envelope in Mara's kitchen drawer, under the takeaway menus. In it, a boy cut out of a photograph with scissors, carefully, a long time ago, so the rest could be shown.
touch: hold "Take the boy out of the envelope" | He's no bigger than your thumb. The scissors went carefully round his cap. The back of him has gone soft as cloth from being held.

@prop q.clearance_order
from: 5
name: The Haldane door
place: q5_haldane_yard
mark: order
tells: household e5_haldane
verb: Look at the door
carries: sight
state: 5 deferred ? has(e5.house_down) | The Haldane door under the headless goat, the bailiffs' orange cross sprayed over the council's pink dot by the frame, and the door still on its hinges, and a light on behind it.
state: 5 boarded ? has(e5.house_cleared) | The Haldane door boarded with ply, screwed in at the corners. The orange cross and the pink dot go on under the board and come out round its edge.
state: 5 crossed ? has(e5.vote_carried) | The Haldane door under the headless goat. By the frame, the council's pink dot from January, and over it now a cross in orange, sprayed fast, a drip run down to the step.
state: 5 dot | The Haldane door under the headless goat. By the frame, a dot of pink paint from the council's can, with a drip run down from it. The black of the damp comes through round the frame.
touch: wipe "Rub at the pink dot" | It doesn't come off. It's the council's good paint. You rub till your thumb is pink and the dot is the same. {sense: e5.paint.spray}

@prop q.shop_window
from: 5
name: The dressed window
place: q5_shop
mark: window
tells: era
carries: heat
state: 5 spoons ? has(e5.house_cleared) | The window dressed for commemoration week: five old bowls, gruel cast in resin, steam from a humidifier under the table. Beside it a jar of wooden spoons from a house clearance off Mill Street, with a price on a string.
state: 5 dressed | The window dressed for commemoration week: five old bowls, gruel cast in resin, steam from a humidifier under the table breathing up between the boards, and a sheaf of wheat laid along the top tied in black ribbon.
touch: press "Put your hand on the glass" | Warm from the lamps inside. Your breath fogs a patch in front of your mouth, and the table goes soft behind it, and comes back.

@prop q.brack_cap
from: 5
name: The cap on the nail
place: q5_brack_kitchen
mark: photo
tells: person e5.leon_c
carries: touch
state: 5 cap ? has(q.tomas_held) | A boy's brown cap on the nail by the back door, beside the wedding photograph with the crack. Gone stiff, the peak cracked across, the band inside dark from a boy's hair a hundred years ago. It has hung there longer than anybody has lived in the house.
state: 5 nail | The nail by the back door, beside the wedding photograph with the crack. A dog lead on it, and no dog.
touch: hold "Take the cap down" ? has(q.tomas_held) | It's small. It would fit a boy of eleven. It smells of nothing now, of the kitchen, of the nail. You hang it back the way it was, peak down. {sense: e5.cap.hold}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- era 5's senses (world/senses.mjs; the shared ones are in senses.lwd)
@sense e5.phone.chime
sound: spoon 0.3 near
caption: a phone chiming
rumble: 0.15 0.35 90
rumble: 0.15 0.35 90 260

@sense e5.voice.note
sound: murmur 0.35 near 2
caption: a voice message playing out of a phone
screen: vignette 0.2 2

@sense e5.clip.sound
sound: murmur 0.25 near 2.4
caption: a small voice out of a phone speaker
screen: vignette 0.4 2.4
hold: 1.2

@sense e5.knee
sound: heart 0.45 under 2.4
caption: your heart, slow and hard
rumble: 0.6 0.05 700
anim: player still 2
hold: 1.2

@sense e5.bodycam
sound: lamphum 0.2 near 2
caption: the small hum of a camera recording
screen: vignette 0.25 3

@sense e5.paint.spray
sound: pour 0.3 near 0.8
caption: paint hissing out of a can
rumble: 0.05 0.3 400

@sense e5.gutter.water
sound: pour 0.75 near 2.6
caption: water coming down a wall in a sheet
rumble: 0.3 0.4 1400
screen: tint #9fb4c8 0.12 2.6
anim: player flinch 0.6

@sense e5.tin.set
sound: thud 0.5 near
caption: a heavy tin set down on a table
rumble: 0.45 0.1 160

@sense e5.tin.open
sound: latch 0.4 near
caption: a tin lid prised up with a thumbnail
rumble: 0.05 0.4 120
camera: push 1.5 1.2
hold: 0.8

@sense e5.edd.splash
sound: thud 0.4 far
sound: pour 0.35 far 1
caption: something heavy going into the river
rumble: 0.2 0.2 300 400
hold: 1.4

@sense e5.cap.hold
sound: breath 0.3 near 2
caption: a long breath in
anim: player tremble 2
rumble: 0.1 0.3 600
camera: push 1.6 1.6
hold: 1.4

@sense e5.digger
sound: chain 0.6 near 2
sound: thud 0.55 near
caption: a digger's bucket going into a stone wall
rumble: 0.7 0.2 500
screen: shake 0.15 0.5

@sense e5.sack.hold
sound: breath 0.2 near 1.6
caption: someone breathing close
rumble: 0.05 0.15 400
camera: push 1.6 1.4
hold: 1

@sense e5.quiet.room
sound: lamphum 0.15 near 3
caption: a fridge humming in a quiet room
screen: dim 0.2 3
hold: 1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- what happened, met in the place (world/echo.mjs)
# Every era 5 fate shows in a place the story brings the player to after it falls (tools/echocheck.mjs).
@echo e5.e.saro
place: q5_saro_flat
when: has(e5.danil_dead)
from: 5
tells: fate f.e5_danil
show: person e4.mira still
show: light dim
line: On the tray of tea glasses one is turned upside down, the one with the gold rim worn off, and nobody turns it back.
sense: e5.quiet.room

@echo e5.e.cert
place: q5_saro_flat
when: has(e5.cert_false)
from: 5
tells: fate f.e5_cert
show: person e4.teo turn
line: Teo keeps getting up to look down into Mill Street, as if somebody is coming up it to tell him what was done to his son. Nobody comes.

@echo e5.e.house
place: q5_mara_flat
when: has(e5.house_cleared)
from: 5
tells: fate f.e5_house
show: person e5.mara still
line: The fair bowl is on a windowsill that isn't its own, in a room that smells of somebody else's paint, with the spider plant's roots still hanging out of the soil.
sense: room.cold

@echo e5.e.wedge
place: q5_archive
when: has(e5.page_torn)
from: 5
tells: fate f.e5_frank
show: sound creak 0.15 near
line: In the front room the old exchange scale hangs level over its two empty pans, done up in new black paint, behind a rope. Nothing has been put under it.

@echo e5.e.sack_lost
place: q5_square
when: has(e5.page_lost)
from: 5
tells: fate f.e5_page_tom
tells: fate f.e5_page_leon
show: sound chain 0.3 far
line: Over the band, from up on the cut, the digger's bucket going into the stone again, where the fold was.

@echo e5.e.sack_kept
place: q5_square
when: has(e5.page_kept)
from: 5
tells: fate f.e5_page_tom
tells: fate f.e5_page_leon
show: person e4.sefa still
line: At the League's end of the square a lad has the oat sack tied to the top of a flagpole, held up over their heads, and the blue goat turns in the wind.

@echo e5.e.cap
place: q5_brack_kitchen
when: has(q.tomas_held) & q_class == militia
from: 5
tells: flag q.tomas_held
line: On the nail by the back door, where it has hung all your life, a boy's brown cap, gone stiff. You wore it to play at police when you were small.
